---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="codehead · agent work in one terminal" description="Write the task with your notes, pick named agents and a branch, then follow and steer the thread in one terminal. codehead runs the agents itself, on Claude Code.">
  <header class="bar">
    <a class="cell first frame" href="/"><span class="logo"><span class="mark">ch</span></span></a>
    <span class="cell grow label">codehead</span>
    <a class="cell frame label" href="/docs/">docs</a>
    <a class="cell frame label" href="https://github.com/hansfuchs/codehead">github</a>
    <button class="cell frame label" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-label="switch theme">◐</button>
  </header>

  <main class="content">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Agent work, in one terminal.</h1>
      <p>
        Write the task with your notes. Pick named agents and a branch. Then follow every message, tool run and
        question of the thread, and steer it, without leaving the terminal. codehead runs the agents itself, on
        Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Goose, Cursor, Pi, Amp and more.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button frame" href="/docs/quick-start/">quick start →</a>
        <a class="button outline frame" href="/docs/">read the docs</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="box">
      <h2 class="box-title">install</h2>
      <pre class="term"><span class="d">$</span> curl -fsSL https://codehead.sh/install | sh</pre>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Linux and macOS · x86_64 and arm64 · needs git and 1 harness: Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Goose, Cursor, Pi, Amp, …</p>
    </section>

    <section class="box" style="margin-top:48px">
      <h2 class="box-title">a thread</h2>
      <pre class="term"><span class="d"> ╭─────╮</span>  <span class="a">ada ★</span>          <span class="d">╭─────╮</span>  <span class="a">bob</span>
<span class="d"> │⢀⢀⢐⢀⢀│</span>  Opus 5.5       <span class="d">│ ⣀⣀⣀ │</span>  Sonnet 5.5
<span class="d"> │  ⢐  │</span>  ▒▓▒ working   <span class="d">│ ⠉⠉⠉ │</span>  idle
<span class="d"> ╰─────╯</span>                 <span class="d">╰─────╯</span>

<span class="r"> you </span> <span class="d">14:02</span>
<span class="a">▌</span> add retries to the webhook sender, then ask @bob for a review

<span class="r"> ada </span> <span class="d">14:02</span>
<span class="d">│</span> <span class="a">▸</span> <span class="d">Read: src/webhook.rs · Edit: src/webhook.rs and 2 more · 4 calls · 21.3s</span>
<span class="d">│</span> Retries are in: 3 tries, backoff 1s / 4s / 16s, only on 5xx and timeouts.
<span class="d">│</span> <span class="a">▸</span> <span class="d">codehead:send: → bob · 1 call · 0.4s</span>

<span class="r"> bob </span> <span class="d">14:04 → ada</span>
<span class="d">┆</span> <span class="d">Looks right. One nit: cap the total wait at 30s.</span>

<span class="d">╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮</span>
<span class="d">│</span><span class="a">›</span> message the thread · @name: an agent · ⌘/ctrl+⏎ sends    <span class="d">│</span>
<span class="d">╰──────────────────────────────────── ▒▓▒ working · esc: interrupt ╯</span></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="grid three">
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">write the task</h2>
        <p>A title, the prompt, notes from your notes folder, context from a Claude Code session. <code>@</code> names agents, <code>&gt;</code> mentions files, notes, threads and skills, paths complete as you type.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">named agents</h2>
        <p>Each agent has a name, a model, a mode, an output style and a 7×4 sprite. 1 TOML file per agent. They message each other and bring each other in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">threads that keep going</h2>
        <p>A thread runs in its own host process: close the terminal, the agents keep working. Open it again from any terminal, branch it, settle it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">questions in the stream</h2>
        <p>Permission requests and agent questions show up in the thread. Answer with ↑↓ and enter, or 1-9. Autopilot, edits, supervised or plan: per agent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">branches and worktrees</h2>
        <p>Work on the current branch, switch, start a new branch, or give the thread its own worktree. The threads tab lists them with unpushed commits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="box-title">plain files</h2>
        <p>A thread is a folder: <code>thread.json</code> and an append-only <code>events.jsonl</code>. Read it, grep it, script it with <code>codehead ctl</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <a class="frame" href="https://github.com/hansfuchs/codehead">github</a>
    <a class="frame" href="/docs/">docs</a>
    <a class="frame" href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
    <span class="grow"></span>
    <span>apache-2.0</span>
  </footer>
</Base>
